#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110302 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110676 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c6914109-37d4-5b87-a64d-f919a124377d" :knowledge-point/title "Graphing Logarithmic Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "cb79d4e2-53ee-5a09-93ad-0b2e1bdc645e" :question/math-academy-id "e-10925" :question/problem "Which of the following plots is the graph of $y = \\log (x)$?\n\n![](images/5f/5f38ded6da0c01657574cf0a40d86d2c5d2ce6b9ff1c29ceaaefbbe82103a277.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall some of the basic properties of $y=\\log (x)$:\n\n- The graph passes through the point $(1,0)$.\n- For $x>1$, the function is positive and grows very slowly as we increase $x$. We say that $y\\rightarrow \\infty$ (slowly) as $x\\rightarrow \\infty$.\n- The domain is $x>0$, and the range is $-\\infty < y < \\infty$. The function is not defined at $x=0$.\n- The function has the vertical asymptote $x=0$.\n- The function is an increasing function.\n\nOf the given plots, the only one that displays all of these properties is II. (For example, plots I, III, and IV all do not have a vertical asymptote $x=0$.)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110303 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110677 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5468f23-98bd-52d9-ba21-85e5eea058a9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Domain and Range of a Logarithmic Function"}] :question/id #uuid "428c177d-8b83-50ad-9840-0dd3ffdf14ee" :question/math-academy-id "e-10926" :question/problem "What are the domain and range of the function $y=\\ln x$?" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the graph of $y = \\ln x$.\n\n![](images/00/004c1050017c1a0631d0dda46c8335248b4f05dad15645513b71e88588d4ed0c.png)\n\nThe domain of $y=\\ln x$ is $x \\in (0,\\infty)$ and the range is $y \\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110304 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110678 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f1fce29-a071-5a86-8a5e-0e7093558d0f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Logarithmic Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "b162bb35-509f-5ed3-896c-19eb9c52deb2" :question/math-academy-id "e-10927" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\ln(x)$?\n\n1. $y\\rightarrow-\\infty$ as $x\\rightarrow 0^+$\n2. The curve passes through the point $(1,0)$\n3. $y\\rightarrow\\infty$ as $x\\rightarrow -\\infty$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's plot the graph of $y=\\ln (x)$.\n\n![](images/d9/d9ca282050c64ffc1ab1950dd6d89288e6d65d680e45bbc9ef29c1a4ae2c3a67.png)\n\nNow, let's consider each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. As $x$ approaches $0^+$, $y$ decreases without bound.\n- Statement II is true. Substituting $x=1$ into the equation of the curve gives a result of $0$:\n$y|= \\ln (1) = 0✓$\n- Statement III is false. The function is not defined for $x<0$, so the function is not defined as $x \\to -\\infty$.\n\nIn conclusion, only statements I and II are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110305 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110679 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "06ede1c9-b17d-504b-86a8-9284f7ded093" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Zeros and Asymptotes of a Logarithmic Function"}] :question/id #uuid "8e8032c5-b7cb-5e25-bc37-0621362ac2fa" :question/math-academy-id "e-10932" :question/problem "What is the vertical asymptote of $y=\\log_{2} x$?" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the graph of\n\n$$\ny=\\log_{2} x\n$$\n\n![](images/96/96d7da4dd7415b769803b9cea8ebf91b65db2ba5afe0249af9d16521eb0f4818.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the function\n\n$$\ny=\\log_{2} x\n$$\n\nhas the vertical asymptote at $x=0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233518 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110679 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "06ede1c9-b17d-504b-86a8-9284f7ded093" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Zeros and Asymptotes of a Logarithmic Function"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "58b2d6c3-6089-5685-8952-ba465d3a1547" :question/math-academy-id "q-156741" :question/problem "Which of the following is a horizontal asymptote of $y={log}_{6}x?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the graph of $y={log}_{6}x.$\n\n![](images/41/4177d9520b3758b29926eba7a7a74ed4c508d861e3c343f46c372ec79500fc9d.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we note that for $x>1$, the graph grows very slowly as we increase $x.$ \n\nWe say that $y\\to \\infty $ (slowly) as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nTherefore, there are no horizontal asymptotes."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233519 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110678 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f1fce29-a071-5a86-8a5e-0e7093558d0f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Logarithmic Functions"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "19c56fe1-1bea-5145-bd09-d55715bd1967" :question/math-academy-id "q-156743" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y={log}_{6}x?$ \n\nI. - It has no zeros\nII. - $y\\to 6$ as $x\\to \\infty $\nIII. - It has a vertical asymptote at $x=0$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y={log}_{6}x.$\n\n![](images/d8/d8d3f9dc995d8801d451b15129860362efa772178cdc3ef07be5adb6a1da5c45.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function has a zero at $x=1.$\n\n- Statement II is false. As $x$ increases, $y$ increases without bound. Therefore, $y\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty $\n\n- Statement III is true.\n\nIn conclusion, only statement III is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111219 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110678 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f1fce29-a071-5a86-8a5e-0e7093558d0f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Logarithmic Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da423ee6-60d2-5fbf-a2a5-c3d103b35222" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186109040} {:answer/id #uuid "ede0e572-2c5a-50de-9e82-7e13932190f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186109041} {:answer/id #uuid "3c6217f0-e9af-5f93-ab26-9dc1352bfdee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186109042} {:answer/id #uuid "41790905-c115-51dd-b040-ce97622db28a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186109043} {:answer/id #uuid "43c9e31a-6391-5c1b-bc12-b2191b613c47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186109044}] :answer-field/id #uuid "a96c92ca-92a4-5c9f-b939-b05afbaad1ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186109039}] :question/id #uuid "dbbb8cfe-8860-58a2-9309-4541390e9f81" :question/math-academy-id "q-47626" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y = \\log x$?\n\n1. The function passes through the point $(1, 0)$\n2. Its horizontal asymptote is $y = 0$.\n3. It passes through the point $(10, 100)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234082 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110677 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5468f23-98bd-52d9-ba21-85e5eea058a9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Domain and Range of a Logarithmic Function"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c872bbea-0830-58ac-9bad-a456f39f833d" :question/math-academy-id "q-47778" :question/problem "What's the range of $f(x)={log}_{9}x?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the graph of $y={log}_{9}x.$\n\n![](images/40/40664f83ba162a93ed06970798d37798db90b85c21d44a9ed20f338df4e1b4e1.png)\n\nThe domain of $y={log}_{9}x$ is $x\\in (0,\\infty )$ and the range is $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"All real numbers.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111382 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110679 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "06ede1c9-b17d-504b-86a8-9284f7ded093" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Zeros and Asymptotes of a Logarithmic Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d162fd51-dc22-55af-af67-6651e200040f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186110018} {:answer/id #uuid "1b1d0a63-831c-5a81-82ba-af5812a26e70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186110019} {:answer/id #uuid "2b2ca5af-5112-5fc5-a29c-bf8dcbd0c25b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186110020} {:answer/id #uuid "4cb287a2-00eb-5f92-afc1-1919b8f8b5fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186110021} {:answer/id #uuid "6fcf43d0-22c7-50ca-a979-2cfa00df8fca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x =-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186110022}] :answer-field/id #uuid "1a86d023-59e1-58b5-8e16-26b22652d4d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186110017}] :question/id #uuid "3ecd0e41-2586-55ce-b89a-08c18fa75672" :question/math-academy-id "q-69657" :question/problem "Which of the following is a zero of $y = \\log_{5} x$?"}]}
